e $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[5]{17-2x}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{17-2x} & =-3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[5]{17-2x})^{5} & =(-3)^{5} \\\\ 17-2x & =-243 \\\\ -2x & =-260 \\\\ x & =130\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=130.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d059c56-ae7f-5fb6-8bc6-2ce97bb7f876" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17baf155-e96d-5274-8ea7-340ef7f9bd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517530} {:answer/id #uuid "3c29c508-ed39-5d19-8512-7d756ca4995b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517606} {:answer/id #uuid "acd1e707-0b6f-5e39-905c-184792e0cf81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The function has no roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517809} {:answer/id #uuid "b07f2caf-1bf7-5a26-ba31-7455fbda5e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517820} {:answer/id #uuid "ea01e92b-e8f5-5231-9823-9b70074e18f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea01e92b-e8f5-5231-9823-9b70074e18f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517931} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8b26ed-f144-5797-9db5-2e62acbf1179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4df596f3-7605-5476-aed1-e33a4f9ad66d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102549" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17} & =15 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{4x+17} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{4x+17})^{4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ 4x+17 & =81 \\\\ 4x & =64 \\\\ x & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt[4]{4\\cdot 16+17}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\sqrt[4]{81}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 3-15 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e6159dd-c12e-5882-be17-815b4cc9ae52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7adc2636-e70e-5248-aa1c-0bb461a58b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adc2636-e70e-5248-aa1c-0bb461a58b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517723} :answer-field/id #uuid "cab81f3e-8bfa-5ab8-83cb-9612dc5b0919" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01c856f3-ee69-579a-9f89-fe0fbee2a037" :question/math-academy-id "q-277239" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x}+2 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{-8-3x} & =-2 \\\\ (\\sqrt[9]{-8-3x})^{9} & =(-2)^{9} \\\\ -8-3x & =-512 \\\\ -3x & =-504 \\\\ x & =168\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=168.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d059c56-ae7f-5fb6-8bc6-2ce97bb7f876" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81b0420-9f65-531f-8353-eb44098ecd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81b0420-9f65-531f-8353-eb44098ecd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517800} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e943489-95ee-51af-889d-7b6b40dcc312" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9219fe2-5911-57bb-89ea-30d2a8256e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-277249" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[4]{3x+15}-3.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the roots of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{3x+15}-3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{3x+15}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{3x+15} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{3x+15})^{4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ 3x+15 & =81 \\\\ 3x & =66 \\\\ x & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{3\\cdot 22+15}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{81}-3 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=22.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d059c56-ae7f-5fb6-8bc6-2ce97bb7f876" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8d030b-747c-50f7-bfed-0d7b9f175406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{33}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517636} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The function has no root" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517787} {:answer/id #uuid "af8f1e2a-1bc1-5f57-a33a-4631f51b1179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517819} {:answer/id #uuid "bde38374-e2a1-5247-9b57-f68cacfb826c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517849} {:answer/id #uuid "fcce51e9-96c5-5943-a86f-056185216518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb6cd66-f41c-5eb6-8461-fb35f552d80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The function has no root" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517787} :answer-field/id #uuid "979c25b1-368c-57a9-a520-1e6925bb31db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "442d41d4-64b6-5c13-9965-e1b753377abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-93093" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{7x+11}+3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{7x+11} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no root."}]}
